{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unicef.org/innovation/femtech%20ventures"}}{\fldrslt 
\f0\fs27 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 UNICEF Femtech Ventures}}
\f0\fs27 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4  is seeking applications to join its second annual cohort of companies using frontier technologies to build open-source solutions for the health, wellbeing, and sexual and reproductive health and rights of girls and women.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb3 Selected companies join the Femtech Ventures portfolio and receive up to US$100,000 in funding, 12 months of technical mentorship and access to UNICEF's global network, including our relationships with governments, to set solutions on pathways to scale.\'a0\'a0\cb1 \
\cb3 If your company is using technologies such as AI, machine learning, blockchain or data science, we want to hear from you.\cb1 \
\cb3 We\'92re especially seeking applications from companies:\uc0\u8239 \cb1 \
\cb3 Registered in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unicefventurefund.org/sites/default/files/2023-08/unicef-programme-country%20%281%29.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \strokec2 UNICEF programme country\uc0\u8239 }}\cb1 \
\cb3 Committed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unicef.org/innovation/stories/unicefs-open-source-approach-innovation#:~:text=Shared%20value%20partnerships%20generating%20open,funding%20for%20open%20source%20solutions."}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \strokec2 Open Source licensing and principles\uc0\u8239 \'a0}}\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb3 Have a functional prototype\uc0\u8239 and results of initial testing\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs45\fsmilli22560 \cf0 \cb3 WOMEN-LED/FOUNDED STARTUPS AND YOUNG FOUNDERS ARE ENCOURAGED TO APPLY\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs33 \cf0 \cb3 Approach to femtech innovation for women and girls\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs27 \cf0 \cb3 Women and girls make up nearly half the world's population, yet women's health receives just six percent of private healthcare investment globally. While technology is rapidly reshaping how health conditions are detected, monitored and treated, women and girls are not benefiting equally from this progress.\'a0\cb1 \
\cb3 The consequences of this underinvestment are felt most acutely in emerging markets, where barriers to quality care are greatest and the women building solutions to address them remain among the least funded. This is not simply a funding gap. It also represents an opportunity for innovation in global healthcare.\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unicef.org/innovation/femtech%20ventures"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 UNICEF Femtech Ventures}}\cb3  is a five-year initiative (2025\'962030) from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unicef.org/innovation/venturefund"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \strokec2 UNICEF Venture Fund}} to invest in locally developed frontier technology solutions that expand access to health, wellbeing, and sexual and reproductive health and rights of girls and women in emerging markets. Building on more than a decade of Venture Fund learning, Femtech Ventures invests in solutions built by companies close to the challenges they address.\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb3 This second call for applications will select the next cohort of Femtech Ventures investees, growing a portfolio of solutions established by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unicef.org/innovation/stories/unicef-backed-femtech-startups-gain-ground-womens-health"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \strokec2 the first cohort}} of 11 companies from eight countries in Africa and Asia.\'a0\cb1 \
\cb3 Central to the Femtech Ventures model is a hyperlocal approach: making systematic, targeted investments in solutions designed within communities, validated in context and built for scale. Safety-by-design is a condition of UNICEF's investment, with companies supported to consider data privacy, consent architecture and user risk from the ground up.\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb3 With the global femtech market projected to reach {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/femtech-market-report"}}{\fldrslt \cf2 \strokec2 US$146 billion by 2033}}, Femtech Ventures is creating space for locally developed solutions to shape a rapidly growing sector while addressing persistent gaps in women\'92s and girls\'92 health.\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs33 \cf0 \cb3 What we're looking for\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs27 \cf0 \cb3 We are looking for companies in emerging markets designing locally grounded solutions with the potential to scale and committed to openness as both a principle and a practice. We believe that inclusive innovation, shaped by a diversity of perspectives and experiences, is essential to creating technologies that respond to local needs.\'a0\cb1 \
\cb3 Femtech Ventures supports both early- and growth-stage companies using frontier technologies such as generative and agentic AI, machine learning and blockchain. We have a particular interest in solutions ready to deploy in low-resource or emergency settings.\'a0\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb3 Through our second call for applications, we are seeking solutions across three pillars:\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs21 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 PILLAR 1-HEALTHCARE ACCESS FOR WOMEN AND GIRLS
\f0\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\fs27 \cf0 \cb3 \strokec4 We are looking for frontier technology that improves health outcomes across the continuum of care, from antenatal and postnatal support to newborn and child health, with a focus on reaching underserved communities with quality care. We are particularly interested in solutions designed for primary and community care, such as:\'a0
\f0\i0 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Point-of-care support tools with automated interpretation of data and/or imagery collected, reducing reliance on visual reads and providing reliable, actionable results for frontline health workers.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Affordable tech-enabled screening tools, especially for conditions that go undetected, such as anaemia, haemoglobinopathies, ferritin status and thyroid function, designed for primary care and community settings.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Novel applications that connect screening, referral and follow-up at the point of care while generating timely, structured intelligence that strengthens planning, policy and accountability at every level of the health system.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Frontier health platforms supporting continuity of care across the maternal health continuum, from conception through the first 1,000 days of a child's life, including remote care in low-bandwidth environments.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Demand forecasting and supply planning tools that ensure essential maternal and child health supplies are available where and when they are needed most, including solutions that integrate staffing, skilling and workload data to strengthen the capacity of community health workers.\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs21 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 PILLAR 2-INFORMED, SAFE AND ACCESSIBLE REPRODUCTIVE HEALTH\'a0
\f0\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\fs27 \cf0 \cb3 \strokec4 We are looking for solutions that give women and girls access to the information, tools and services they need to understand and manage their sexual and reproductive health, particularly where it is limited by stigma, distance, cost or restricted mobility. Solutions should strengthen informed decision-making, privacy and control over personal health data. We seek solutions such as:\'a0
\f0\i0 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 AI-powered accessible platforms delivering personalized reproductive health information and counselling in underserved languages, especially for low-literacy and low-bandwidth environments.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Community health worker platforms that extend the reach of sexual and reproductive health and rights services through frontline workers, with interoperable digital tools for case management, referral and follow-up.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Frontier technology applications for improving the detection and screening of HPV and the delivery of prevention services in primary and community healthcare, designed for the realities of low-resource health systems.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Tech-enabled platforms that facilitate access to finance for sexual and reproductive healthcare, connecting women and girls to services through innovations in health coverage.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Consent- and privacy-preserving data solutions that allow women and girls to control how sensitive reproductive health information is collected and used.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs21 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 PILLAR 3-MENTAL WELLBEING, SAFETY AND PROTECTION \uc0\u8239 \u8239 
\f0\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\fs27 \cf0 \cb3 \strokec4 We are looking for innovations that address the psychological, emotional and digital safety needs of women, girls and children, including solutions tackling gender-based violence, online harm and abuse, trauma response, and maternal and adolescent mental health, such as:
\f0\i0 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Digital mental health tools providing accessible, culturally appropriate psychosocial support for women, adolescent girls and children, especially interoperable solutions that integrate maternal mental health screening into existing systems such as DHIS2.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Digital decision-support tools that equip community health workers to identify risks, including those related to maternal mental health, deliver evidence-based interventions and determine when specialist referral is needed.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 AI-enabled platforms for the early detection of and response to gender-based violence, including safe reporting mechanisms, access to information and referral to support services.\'a0\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Online safety tools that identify, flag and respond to digital abuse, harassment and exploitation targeting women and girls, including through social media monitoring and AI-based detection systems.\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Community-level tools that train and support frontline workers, including teachers, community health workers and social workers, to identify risks and respond to the mental health needs of women and children.\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs21 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 +WE ARE ACTIVELY SEEKING COMPANIES THAT PUSH THE BOUNDARIES OF FRONTIER TECHNOLOGIES IN INNOVATIVE AND SCALABLE WAYS WITH GLOBAL RELEVANCE. IF YOU THINK YOU MEET THESE CRITERIA,\uc0\u8239 WE WANT TO HEAR FROM YOU.\'a0\cb1 \
